Now game.js changes: import drawWeather; canPlace pads; snap; render call.

canPlace decor loop: skip `d.zone === 'pad'`. Also explicit placement rule? Map.placement = 'pads-or-water' → water default. We can add comment. And snapping in placeTower.

Snap: compute nx/ny; if map.buildPads, find nearest within r*0.62 and snap to its center → tower.x based on nx*this.w. But obstruction check was done at original position; snapped position may be closer to path? Pads are safe. Fine. Also if on pad edge, snapping helps.

Implement:
```js
placeTower(type, nx, ny) {
  let px = nx, py = ny;
  const pads = this.map.buildPads;
  if (pads) {
    for (const p of pads) {
      const d = Math.hypot(nx - p.x, ny - p.y);
      if (d <= p.r * 0.7) { px = p.x; py = p.y; break; }
    }
  }
  const check = this.canPlace(type, px, py);
  ...
  tower = {..., nx: px, ny: py, x: px*w ...}
```
But canPlace called with snapped coords after we already validated? Do snap first then check. Good.

Also preview: hover placement won't snap, minor mismatch. Could snap in canPlace? No. It's okay; previews at cursor. Actually preview validity uses canPlace at cursor. Since pads are valid anyway, fine.

Rain render after effects.

Import update.

