Now CSS. Add `.send-hold` styles and auto styles after `.send-btn.in-wave small`.

Design:

```
.send-hold {
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  width: 0;
  height: 3px;
  border-radius: 0 999px 999px 0;
  background: rgba(255, 249, 220, 0.95);
  opacity: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  transition: width 0.6s linear, opacity 0.15s;
}
.send-btn.holding .send-hold { width: 100%; opacity: 1; }
.send-btn.hold-ready .send-hold { background: #fff6c8; box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255, 240, 170, 0.9); }
.send-btn.auto {
  border-color: #bfe9a8;
  color: #14230d;
  background:
    linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.28), transparent 42%),
    linear-gradient(180deg, #a9dd86, #6aab48);
  box-shadow: 0 3px 0 #3f6d27, 0 7px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.3), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.45);
}
.send-btn.auto .send-hold { width: 100%; opacity: 1; background: #d8f7c4; box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(180, 245, 140, .85); }
.send-btn.auto:hover { filter: brightness(1.06); }
.send-btn.auto.in-wave {
  border-color: rgba(170, 226, 140, 0.6);
  color: #e1f4d5;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #3a5a2d, #21371a);
  box-shadow: 0 2px 0 #12210c, inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.08), 0 0 18px rgba(132, 214, 96, .14);
  cursor: pointer;
}
.send-btn.auto.in-wave small { opacity: .78; }
.send-btn.auto::after { display: none; }
```

Wait, the auto button in build should still allow click to stop, so it should look clickable. Green. Fine.

`user-select:none` and `touch-action:manipulation` on `.send-btn`. Add to base `.send-btn`.

Also `.send-btn:active` currently translate; with hold it still depresses. Fine.

Potential CSS specificity issue: `.send-btn.auto` comes after `.send-btn.in-wave` in the file? We'll add after `.send-btn.in-wave small`, which is after `.send-btn.in-wave`, so auto rules override. The `.send-btn.auto.in-wave` rule after that overrides auto. Good.

The `send-hold` element inside the button is `<i>` with default `font-style: italic`, irrelevant. `display` default inline; position absolute makes it block.

Also `z-index`? The bar at bottom, the sheen `::after` may draw on top; okay. Set `z-index: 2` and `::after` z-index 0? Pseudo elements are painted after child content? In stacking order, ::after is after children. But the sheen is translucent. No issue. The bar will still show at bottom.

Let's add.

